{"id":"tur-t1-0011","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"price.bill","domain":3,"text_native":"Hesap lütfen.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"The bill, please.","source_caption":"The check, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Where the word for bill and the word for receipt are the same word and neither is 'account'.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0012","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"price.card-ok","domain":3,"text_native":"Kredi kartı geçerli mi?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Is card payment accepted?","source_caption":"Do you accept credit cards?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The alternative to carrying cash, and the question that decides whether you are standing in a queue that moves.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0013","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"price.how-much","domain":3,"text_native":"Bunun fiyatı nedir?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"How much is this?","source_caption":"How much is this?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most useful question in the tier, and the one people are most afraid to ask. It is not rude anywhere.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0014","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-cheap","domain":3,"text_native":"ucuz","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"It is cheaper in my country.","source_caption":"Cheap","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Read as an accusation almost everywhere. Included because knowing that it is an accusation is worth more than being able to say it politely.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0015","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-expensive","domain":3,"text_native":"pahalı","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"That is too expensive.","source_caption":"Expensive","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Used with the hand gesture that accompanies it. The gesture carries the meaning and the word confirms it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0016","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"money.atm","domain":3,"text_native":"ATM/Bankamatik nerede?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Where is an ATM?","source_caption":"Where is an automatic teller machine (ATM)?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognising rather than producing it: you will be shown the sign rather than expected to ask.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0017","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"money.change","domain":3,"text_native":"Benim için para bozabilir misiniz?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please change this into local money.","source_caption":"Can you change money for me?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The word 'change' means both coins and alteration in several of these languages, and the wrong one is confusing.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0018","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"money.exchange-rate","domain":3,"text_native":"Döviz kuru nedir?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"What is the exchange rate?","source_caption":"What is the exchange rate?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Often answered by pointing at a board rather than spoken.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0019","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"money.keep-change","domain":3,"text_native":"Üstü kalsın.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please keep the change.","source_caption":"Keep the change.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Refusing loose coins is often faster and always understood.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba tur-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"357217","author":"plover"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0020","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"toilet.where","domain":12,"text_native":"Tuvalet nerede?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Where is the toilet?","source_caption":"Where is the toilet?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most urgent question in this tier and the one every phrasebook leads with. In several languages the word is the only one a traveller needs for years.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0021","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"food.bill-restaurant","domain":4,"text_native":"Hesap, lütfen.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Can we have the bill here, please?","source_caption":"The bill, please!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Sometimes distinct from the shop bill in the same language, and using the wrong one reads as asking to pay before finishing.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba tur-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"1116121","author":"atitarev"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0022","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"food.menu","domain":4,"text_native":"Menüye bakabilir miyim?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"The menu, please.","source_caption":"Can I look at the menu, please?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"One question covers a whole meal. Most phrasebooks waste slots on individual dishes instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0023","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"food.no-meat","domain":4,"text_native":"Domuz eti yemem.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I do not eat meat.","source_caption":"I don't eat pork.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Saying it once at the start of the trip saves a refusal at the table, where it is awkward for both sides.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0024","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"food.water","domain":4,"text_native":"su","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Water, please.","source_caption":"water","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Refusing the water in a restaurant is a small discourtesy in several of these countries. This is how to ask for some instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0025","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"way.straight","domain":7,"text_native":"Dümdüz gidin.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Go straight ahead.","source_caption":"Go straight ahead.","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba tur-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"1256061","author":"CK"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0026","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-left","domain":7,"text_native":"sol","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Turn left.","source_caption":"Left","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced: you are the one being given directions far more often than giving them.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0027","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-right","domain":7,"text_native":"sağ","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Turn right.","source_caption":"Right","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0028","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"stay.checkout","domain":5,"text_native":"Çıkış yapıyorum.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I would like to check out, please.","source_caption":"I want to check out.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said the morning before leaving, so the bill is not waiting at the desk while luggage is being gathered.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0029","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"stay.room","domain":5,"text_native":"Rezervasyon yaptırmıştım.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I have a room booked.","source_caption":"I have a reservation.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The opening line at a front desk, and the word that gets you past it is the name on the booking.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba tur-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"1267347","author":"CK"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0030","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"move.destination","domain":6,"text_native":"Beni oraya götürün, lütfen.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please take me there.","source_caption":"Take me there, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Shown with a map or a written address while saying it. 'There' is the word the pages use; 'this address' is in none of them, and a slot phrased from imagination rather than from a caption is a slot that can never be filled.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0031","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"move.taxi","domain":6,"text_native":"Lütfen bana bir taksi çağır.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please call me a taxi.","source_caption":"Please call me a taxi.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Hailed rather than called in most of these countries, but asking produces one more option.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba tur-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"6931493","author":"CK"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0032","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"move.ticket","domain":6,"text_native":"Bir bilet istiyorum, lütfen.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"One ticket to","source_caption":"I'd like one ticket, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Ordering the number and the destination together, which is the whole transaction.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba tur-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"5459868","author":"mailohilohi"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0033","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"move.where-is-platform","domain":6,"text_native":"O hangi platformda?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Which platform?","source_caption":"Which platform is it on?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Answered by a sign or a display more often than by a person.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba tur-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"4454042","author":"CM"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0034","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"shop.size","domain":8,"text_native":"Daha küçük bir boyutu olan var mı?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Do you have a smaller size?","source_caption":"Do you have a smaller size?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Clothing sizes are not comparable across countries, so asking beats estimating.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba tur-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"1308075","author":"CK"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0035","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"health.doctor","domain":9,"text_native":"Bir doktora ihtiyacım var.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I need a doctor.","source_caption":"I need a doctor.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Short enough to say to anyone, which is the point — a phrase you cannot finish is a phrase that arrives too late.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0036","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"health.hospital","domain":9,"text_native":"En yakın hastane nerede?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Where is the nearest hospital?","source_caption":"Where is the closest hospital?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asked of a passer-by rather than declared to a driver. The pages carry the question and not the instruction to be driven, which is a different conversation with a different person.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba tur-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"2710796","author":"KoreanBeaver"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0037","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"health.hurt","domain":9,"text_native":"Yaralandım.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I have been injured.","source_caption":"I've been injured.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Declares the situation before being asked. Several of these languages change tense or register on the word for injury, and the flat version sounds like a complaint.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0038","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"help.dont-touch","domain":10,"text_native":"Bana dokunma!","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Do not touch me.","source_caption":"Don't touch me!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Out loud and to a person, not shouted generally. Several of these languages treat it as an accusation, so it is a sentence to use deliberately.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0039","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"help.emergency","domain":10,"text_native":"Acil durum.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"It is an emergency.","source_caption":"It's an emergency.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Changes how the next thirty seconds go. Two words, and in several of these languages it reaches a different set of responses than a request would.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0040","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"help.leave-me-alone","domain":10,"text_native":"Beni yalnız bırak.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please leave me alone.","source_caption":"Leave me alone.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said firmly and quietly. Raising the volume is what turns it from a boundary into an incident in several of these cultures.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0041","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"help.lost","domain":10,"text_native":"Kayboldum.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I am lost.","source_caption":"I'm lost.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asking a passer-by for help is a separate skill from reading a sign, and it uses different vocabulary in every one of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0042","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"help.phone","domain":10,"text_native":"Telefonunuzu kullanabilir miyim?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Can I use your phone?","source_caption":"Can I use your phone?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most common thing a traveller needs that a phone provides, and asking a stranger for it is usually granted.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0043","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"help.police","domain":10,"text_native":"Polisi arayacağım.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please call the police.","source_caption":"I'll call the police.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Usually needs a phone, and in most places a local number rather than an international one.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tur-t1-0044","lang":"tur","tier":1,"slot":"help.thief","domain":10,"text_native":"Dur! Hırsız!","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Stop, thief!","source_caption":"Stop! Thief!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Loud, and aimed at a crowd rather than at one person. Included because the vocabulary exists and because it is the sentence that makes people nearby move.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Turkish phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Turkish_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
